WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.830
In the ancient world, a herald would stand in
a public place and cry out an announcement.

2
00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:10.790
Scholars use a Greek word from that cry
for the first Christians' public message:

3
00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:12.030
kerygma.

4
00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.990
The book of Acts gives Peter's
speeches to crowds in Jerusalem.

5
00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:19.280
Did the first Christians
all preach the same message?

6
00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:22.270
And are these really Peter's own words?

7
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.190
In this mission, you'll
test a famous claim:

8
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.460
that one pattern runs through
the earliest preaching.

9
00:00:28.510 --> 00:00:32.480
Then you'll weigh up whether the
speeches have historical value.

10
00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:36.970
Your mission: find out whether the
first Christians shared one message,

11
00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:39.160
and whose words these speeches are.
